BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:httpswwwvisitfrederickorgeventjumbospumpkinpatchfallfestival11483-20261009@visitfrederick
DTSTAMP:20261009T165624Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261009
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261010
SUMMARY:Jumbo's Pumpkin Patch Fall Festival
DESCRIPTION:Celebrate the season with a full day of festive fun for all ages at Jumbo’s Pumpkin Patch! From classic farm adventures to fall-themed attractions\, our Fall Fun Festival is the perfect weekend outing for families\, friends\, and pumpkin lovers. What’s Included with Admission: Your ticket includes unlimited access to a variety of seasonal attractions: Hayrides through the farm 30+ acre u-pick pumpkin patch (pumpkins sold by the pound) Corn maze (14 acres) Petting zoo Jumping pillow Giant slides Mini mazes for younger guests Playgrounds and yard games General Store with fall shopping and décor​ Optional Add-Ons: (Available for Purchase Onsite - Saturday and Sunday Only) Enhance your day with these fun extras: Pony Rides – $7 Face Painting – $4 Sandy Candy (Edible Sand Art) – $4 Corn Cannon – $5 (3 shots) ​ Food & Drinks: Come hungry! A variety of food\, snacks\, and beverages are available for purchase\, including selections from Liquidity Ale Works of Mt. Airy. Tickets available online or at the gate.
URL:https://www.visitfrederick.org/event/jumbos-pumpkin-patch-fall-festival/11483/
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:httpswwwvisitfrederickorgeventlegends26lore26224-20261009@visitfrederick
DTSTAMP:20261009T165624Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261009
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261031
SUMMARY:Legends & Lore
DESCRIPTION:Come see the darker side of Frederick. When night falls\, Frederick’s familiar streets have rather different stories to tell. Climb aboard our vintage double-decker for an hour of dark tales from Frederick’s past\, researched from local histories\, old accounts and the legends that have lingered long after the people involved have gone. As we make our way through the city\, we’ll slow down at the very places connected to these stories\, from historic streets and old buildings to some of Frederick’s more famously haunted places. Along the way\, you’ll hear tales of strange happenings\, restless spirits and the darker chapters of local history\, all told against the backdrop of Frederick after dark. And because it’s October\, you’ll also get a rather good view from the top deck as the city’s historic homes and neighborhoods put on their best autumn and Halloween displays. Whether you’re a believer\, a skeptic\, or simply enjoy a good story with a slightly unsettling ending\, Legends and Lore offers a different way to discover Frederick’s history. Just remember\, it’s much easier to laugh at a ghost story when you’re not sitting on the top deck in the dark. TOUR HIGHLIGHTS Hear researched tales of Frederick’s haunted places\, local legends and darker history\, told where the stories happened. Experience Frederick after dark from the top deck\, with historic streets\, autumn displays and a few places you’ll look at rather differently afterwards. TOUR DETAILS Price: $35 per person Duration: 1 hour Recommended Age: 14+ Departure: RAK Brewing Co\, 400 Sagner Ave\, Frederick\, MD\, 21701
URL:https://www.visitfrederick.org/event/legends-%26-lore/26224/
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:httpswwwvisitfrederickorgeventthehotsardines25956-20261009@visitfrederick
DTSTAMP:20261009T165624Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261009
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261010
SUMMARY:The Hot Sardines
DESCRIPTION:Emerging a decade ago from the underground parties of Brooklyn to touring worldwide and recording a string of albums that have racked up more than 60 million streams\, The Hot Sardines’ own “potent and assured” ( The New York Times )\, “simply phenomenal” ( The Times \, London) brand of reinvigorated classic jazz landed them at the center of a whirlwind. In 2024\, co-founders Elizabeth Bougerol (vocals) and Evan Palazzo (piano) debuted the Sardines’ new project at Carnegie Hall\, selling out within hours. Banned Jazz is a celebration of joy as an act of resistance and the unifying power of music\, recounting how political forces in the U.S. and Europe tried (and failed) to suppress the music of Louis Armstrong\, Josephine Baker\, Benny Goodman\, and more with its messages of cultural\, racial\, and sexual freedom. The Sardines’ latest recording is C’est La Vie \, a bilingual affair of vintage jazz standards and originals. The title track\, a Bossa nova original in French\, is a timely ode to fully living each moment\, even when you don’t know what the next will bring. The Hot Sardines continue to tour\, taking Banned Jazz on the road starting in 2025\, and continuing into 2026. Learn more about the band on their official website. This show is part of the Weinberg Center’s Centennial Events\, celebrating 100 years of entertainment in our historic building. The Weinberg Center\, located in the heart of Downtown Frederick\, MD\, offers a historic backdrop and timeless atmosphere for a meaningful entertainment experience.
URL:https://www.visitfrederick.org/event/the-hot-sardines/25956/
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:httpswwwvisitfrederickorgeventthesubmensaswspecialguestspunkshow26217-20261009@visitfrederick
DTSTAMP:20261009T165624Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261009
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261010
SUMMARY:The SUBMENSAS w/ special guests PUNK Show
DESCRIPTION:The longest-running punk act in the DMV comes to Rockwell Brewery w/special guests on October 9th\, 2026 @ 7:30PM Formed in 1983 out of DMV’s underground punk circuit\, The Submensas have spent decades evolving without ever fully disappearing. Now\, with a steady stream of new releases that draw from influences as diverse as funk to dark country\, The Submensas have found a new relevance in the world of today. The band’s line-up itself is a collision of 1980s underground veterans: drummer Darryl Dardenne (Pony Fight)\, bassist Vernon Hawkins (Sex on TV) and Jim Mcpherson (The Platinum Slugs)\, all with roots in the band’s original era. Damon Norko\, who fronts the band\, is also a local English teacher. Says S.D. Price in the Frederick News Post: “Their cross-generational appeal has become one of the most unexpected elements of the band’s current run. What began as a product of the 1980s underground has found new life with younger listeners\, while still resonating with those who were there the first time around. It is a dynamic that speaks to something deeper than nostalgia. At its core\, The Submensas’ music is rooted in themes that have not gone away: frustration\, fairness\, and the search for meaning in systems that often feel stacked against the individual. \\
URL:https://www.visitfrederick.org/event/the-submensas-w-special-guests-punk-show/26217/
END:VEVENT
