DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261026
SUMMARY:Blooms and Bovines | Highland Cows + Pumpkin Floral Centerpiece Event
DESCRIPTION:Blooms & Bovines: Fall Edition I can easily argue that fall on the farm is one of our favorite seasons - and this event is a big reason why!! “Blooms & Bovines: Fall Edition” is all about pumpkins\, florals and getting hands on with Highland cows! Your 1.5 hour time-slot on the farm will include: One pie pumpkin (varieties/colors will vary\, you get your pick!) A DIY flower bar to create a floral centerpiece with your pumpkin Hands on time with real life highland cows Photo opportunity with highland calf at our fall themed backdrop All flowers\, clippers cow brushes and supplies are included During the 1.5 hour time-slot on the farm\, the cows will be available for brushing for the first hour ONLY. The cows will be on break the remaining 30 minutes of your experience- the perfect time to finish your pumpkin centerpiece! $45/ticket - pre purchased tickets required. Every individual ages 4+ are required to have their own ticket regardless of participation level. Questions? Victoria at blackrockhighlands@gmail.com
URL:https://www.visitfrederick.org/event/blooms-and-bovines-%7c-highland-cows-%2b-pumpkin-floral-centerpiece-event/25730/
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:httpswwwvisitfrederickorgeventcatoctincolorfest7331-20261010@visitfrederick
DTSTAMP:20261009T165624Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261010
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261012
SUMMARY:Catoctin Colorfest
DESCRIPTION:Colorfest\, established in 1963\, is one of the largest outdoor craft shows on the East Coast! The Colorfest is not just an event\, but an experience. Amazing crafts\, art\, jewelry\, clothing\, and a variety of delicious food are located throughout town. Demonstrations by various crafters will be taking place throughout the two days. Admission is free to Colorfest\, but a fee is charged at the parking locations throughout the town. Please click here for additional information. This event is rain or shine.
URL:https://www.visitfrederick.org/event/catoctin-colorfest/7331/
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:httpswwwvisitfrederickorgeventchannelzero26201-20261010@visitfrederick
DTSTAMP:20261009T165624Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261010
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261011
SUMMARY:Channel Zero
DESCRIPTION:Your favorite Frederick darkwave DJ night is BACK featuring a Vacant Windows headline among a four DJ lineup. Dance the night away to beats inspired by postpunk hits\; think Depeche Mode\, Duran Duran\, Joy Division\, The Smiths\; and mixed in with the goth industrialism of Skinny Puppy and Ministry - the very essence of 80s era darkwave! So get dancing! We’re going ‘til midnight. The vibes don’t just end on the dance floor - take a break with a tarot reading in the lounge. Embrace the darkness.
URL:https://www.visitfrederick.org/event/channel-zero/26201/
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:httpswwwvisitfrederickorgeventdavidsedaris25975-20261010@visitfrederick
DTSTAMP:20261009T165624Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261010
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261011
SUMMARY:David Sedaris
DESCRIPTION:David Sedaris is one of America’s pre-eminent humor writers. He is a master of satire and one of today’s most observant authors. Beloved for his personal essays and short stories\, David Sedaris is the author of the New York Times bestsellers Barrel Fever \, Holidays on Ice \, Naked\, Me Talk Pretty One Day\, Dress Your Family in Corduroy and Denim \, When You Are Engulfed in Flames\, Let’s Explore Diabetes with Owls\, Calypso\, and Happy-Go-Lucky . The audio version of Happy-Go-Lucky \, written and narrated by Sedaris\, won the 2023 Audie Award. His book The Best of Me \, collects 42 previously published stories and essays. Sedaris also wrote Squirrel Seeks Chipmunk: A Modest Bestiary\, a collection of fables with illustrations by Ian Falconer. His next book of essays will be The Land and Its People (Back Bay Books\, May 26\, 2026). For this event\, Sedaris will deliver a 60-minute reading followed by questions from the audience. Learn more about the author on his official website. This show is part of the Weinberg Center’s LIVE! Series\, celebrating iconic authors and speakers. The Weinberg Center\, located in the heart of Downtown Frederick\, MD\, offers a historic backdrop and excellent setting for a memorable speaker experience.
URL:https://www.visitfrederick.org/event/david-sedaris/25975/
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:httpswwwvisitfrederickorgeventexpressivecharcoalforbeginners26215-20261010@visitfrederick
DTSTAMP:20261009T165624Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261010
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261011
SUMMARY:Expressive Charcoal for Beginners
DESCRIPTION:Step into the studio for an immersive\, hands-on exploration of charcoal. Charcoal is one of the most immediate\, versatile\, and tactile drawing mediums\, making it ideal for letting go of perfectionism and embracing intuitive expression. In this workshop\, artist Emily Johnson will guide students through dynamic mark-making\, building deep contrast\, and using erasure and layering to create rich\, atmospheric drawings. We will explore continuous-line exercises\, gestural warm-ups\, and techniques for capturing energy\, form\, and texture rather than rigid representation. What to Bring: Everything provided. Experience Level: Designed for all experience levels—from curious beginners to practicing artists wanting to loosen up their style—this class emphasizes the pleasure of the physical process and discovering your authentic visual language in a relaxed\, encouraging environment. Ages 12+.
URL:https://www.visitfrederick.org/event/expressive-charcoal-for-beginners/26215/
END:VEVENT
